  "description": "Overview Put your AI knowledge to the test! Claude Build Challenge 2026 is a fast-paced online quiz designed for students, developers, and tech enthusiasts to showcase their understanding of Claude AI, generative AI fundamentals, and prompt engineering. About the Quiz This challenge is a straightforward, knowledge-based competition focused on speed and accuracy. Whether you are just getting started with AI or actively exploring large language models, this quiz is a great way to benchmark your skills and earn recognition. Quiz Format & Details Mode: Online (hosted on Unstop) Participation: Individual (Solo) Format: Multiple Choice Questions (MCQs) Eligibility: Open to all undergraduate/postgraduate students and tech enthusiasts. Rules & Guidelines All participants must complete the quiz within the given time window. Each question carries equal weightage, with no negative marking (update if applicable). Tie-Breaker: In case of a tie in scores, the participant who finishes in less time will be ranked higher. Participants can only attempt the quiz once; multiple entries will lead to disqualification. The decision of the organizing team will be final and binding. Rewards & Certificates Winners: Winner Certificates Participation: Verified Participation Certificates for all participants who successfully complete the quiz.",
